# PART 3 — DOCKER DEPLOYMENT

The application must be deployable using Docker Compose.

Suggested configuration:

```yaml
services:
  comfyui-gallery:
    build: .
    container_name: comfyui-gallery
    restart: unless-stopped

    ports:
      - "8080:8080"

    environment:
      COMFYUI_URL: "http://comfyui:8188"
      COMFYUI_OUTPUT_DIR: "/data/output"
      COMFYUI_MODELS_DIR: "/data/models"
      DATABASE_PATH: "/app/data/gallery.db"
      THUMBNAIL_PATH: "/app/data/thumbnails"

    volumes:
      - /path/to/comfyui/output:/data/output:ro
      - /path/to/comfyui/models:/data/models:ro
      - ./gallery-data:/app/data
      - ./model-downloads:/downloads
```

Deployment requirements:

- The ComfyUI output directory must be mounted read-only.
- The model directory should initially be mounted read-only.
- Model downloads must use a configurable writable destination.
- Database and thumbnails must persist across container restarts.
- All paths and connection URLs must be configurable.
- ComfyUI does not need to run in the same Docker Compose project.
- Support connections to ComfyUI on another Docker host or LAN machine.
- Include a connection test button.
- Do not require access to the Docker socket.

Document all environment variables, volume mounts, configuration options, and upgrade procedures.

