# PART 6 — METADATA EXTRACTION

This is one of the foundational components of the application.

Extract as much information as possible from image metadata.

## 6.1 Generation metadata

Extract:

- Positive prompt.
- Negative prompt.
- Seed.
- Steps.
- CFG.
- Sampler.
- Scheduler.
- Width and height.
- Denoise.
- Batch information.
- Generation date, if available.
- Checkpoint.
- VAE.
- All LoRAs.
- LoRA strengths.
- CLIP strengths.
- Other model dependencies.

## 6.2 Workflow metadata

Store these independently:

1. Original embedded metadata.
2. Visual ComfyUI workflow JSON.
3. API-format workflow JSON.
4. Parsed generation parameters.
5. Extracted model dependencies.

Never discard unknown metadata.

Preserve original workflow JSON as an immutable historical record.

Build an extensible parser architecture that can support additional metadata formats later.

When metadata is incomplete, explicitly identify which fields could not be extracted.

Do not invent missing metadata.

## 6.3 LoRA extraction

This functionality deserves special attention.

Support:

- Multiple LoRA loader nodes.
- Multiple LoRAs per image.
- Separate model and CLIP strengths.
- Different loader node types.
- LoRA names and paths.
- Model hashes when available.

Never assume that LoRAs can be identified exclusively through the positive prompt.

The visual workflow is an important source of information.

Use workflow node inspection and embedded metadata together, while preserving the provenance of extracted information.

