# PART 10 — REPRODUCIBILITY AND DEPENDENCY CHECKER

Every image should receive a dependency status.

Use these statuses:

| Status | Meaning |
|---|---|
| Exact match | All verifiable model hashes match |
| Available | Required models are present, but identity is not fully verified |
| Incomplete | One or more dependencies are missing |
| Unknown | Insufficient metadata |

When a model is missing, display:

- Model name.
- Model type.
- Historical file path.
- Hash, if available.
- Number of images depending on it.
- Whether a download source is known.

Create a Missing Dependencies dashboard.

Allow users to select multiple missing dependencies and locate them together.

Clearly distinguish between:

- Missing models.
- Models that exist but have unverified identities.
- Models verified through hashes.
- Dependencies that cannot be determined.

