# PART 15 — ADDITIONAL FEATURES TO INCLUDE

These five features should be incorporated into the architecture and implemented as part of the appropriate development phases.

## 15.1 Independent workflow library

A workflow should be retainable independently of its generated images.

Allow users to:

- Save workflows separately.
- Give workflows custom names.
- Store original workflow JSON.
- Associate multiple images with one workflow.
- Browse and manage saved workflows.

Deleting or moving an image must not automatically delete its associated saved workflow.

## 15.2 Model usage impact report

Before removing a LoRA or checkpoint, show:

- Number of images that depend on it.
- Number of workflows that depend on it.
- Related historical generations.

This will help users safely manage their model collection.

## 15.3 Metadata confidence and provenance

Distinguish between:

- Information extracted directly from embedded metadata.
- Information extracted from workflow nodes.
- Information inferred from external model inventories.
- Information that could not be verified.

Avoid presenting inferred information as confirmed facts.

## 15.4 Database backup and restore

Provide an easy-to-use backup interface.

Include:

- Manual database backup.
- Restore functionality.
- Export of ratings, tags, collections, and annotations.
- Scheduled backup capability.
- Clear backup status and error reporting.

## 15.5 Generation history

Track reproductions launched from the gallery.

Record:

- Original image.
- Workflow used.
- Submission date.
- ComfyUI prompt ID.
- Success or failure status.
- Execution errors.
- Resulting images.

This should create a useful feedback loop between the gallery and ComfyUI.

